    "searchCoverage": "Official AWS STS AssumeRole requires Signature Version 4. Pinned executors import signAwsSigV4Request and POST to https://sts.${region}.amazonaws.com/. The credential validator does not call STS. Dated incident search on 2026-09-13 found customer-account STS usage in unrelated compromises and a patched AWS SDK hostname-injection class; no current unresolved STS service-platform compromise is asserted.",
    "incidents": [
      {
        "incidentDate": "2025-10-14",
        "disclosureDate": "2026-01-08",
        "affectedProduct": "AWS SDKs hostname construction (CVE-2026-22611 class)",
        "affectedData": "Malformed region values could redirect a signed STS request; AWS patched SDKs. Not an STS service-platform compromise.",
        "status": "historical SDK defect; patched",
        "source": "https://siliconangle.com/2026/08/24/aws-patches-sdk-flaw-that-turned-a-region-field-into-credential-theft/",
        "remediation": "AWS patched affected SDKs beginning January 2026.",
        "residualRisk": "Signing and computed regional hosts remain unsupported in native templates regardless of SDK patch state."
      }
    ],
    "remainingGates": [
      "operationQuality: pinned OpenConnector signs every STS request with AWS Signature Version 4 (signAwsSigV4Request). Native templates cannot compute SigV4 headers. Official AssumeRole Query API requires AUTHPARAMS / SigV4.",
      "boundedNetwork: pinned source computes https://sts.${region}.amazonaws.com with default region ap-southeast-1. Region is not a required stored id plus bounded wildcard covering official regional STS hosts. The global example host sts.amazonaws.com is used only so the recipe has a native shape; it is not an admitted unsigned endpoint.",
      "credentials: there is no cheap authenticated read. The pinned credential validator is a local field check. The only upstream action is AssumeRole, which issues temporary credentials.",
      "live authentication unverified"
